      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "If you optimize avatar for Quest side (needs Android package in Unity) it will show both \"PC +Quest\" icon. Because PC is always enabled on all avatars.\n\nQuest will only lit if it's exported with Android platform SDK.\n\nIn nameplate it should show it if avatar is both PC/Quest compatible. Then it will lit both up. If your avatar is PC only, it will only lit PC part and Quest users will see you have PC-only avatar, so that explained why they will see \"PC\" default loading avatar model.\n\nBut of course the icon must also same as in the menu listing, not different!\n\nIt's only because the avatar itself is compatible, NOT where you coming from. If Quest user plays, it will lit both sides.\n\nI understand it's bit confusing. Quest users can only use Quest compatible avatar, but it will just lit PC/Quest because the avatar is also playable for PC side.\n\nIf we want see where he is coming from, then double circles (blue/green) is not needed and only ONE colored circle is needed. PC users will have for example BLUE dot, Quest users have GREEN dot below.\n\nBut for now, it's purely only for avatar compatibility... not where users is coming from.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
